dlm Fortran translation - notices and provenance

Upstream package: dlm
Upstream version: 1.1-6.1
Upstream title: Bayesian and Likelihood Analysis of Dynamic Linear Models
Upstream author/maintainer attribution from DESCRIPTION:
  Giovanni Petris - author and maintainer
  Wally Gilks - contributor; original C code for ARMS
Upstream license: GPL (>= 2)

This directory is a clean-room language translation of computational portions
of the upstream R package. The original R sources used for provenance are kept
under provenance/upstream and are not compiled by FPM. Plotting, printing,
interactive progress interfaces, R S3/list construction, R time-series
metadata, and formula handling are outside the Fortran runtime interface. R
closures and optimizer result lists are represented by typed Fortran objects.

The ARMS implementation in `src/dlm_arms.f90` is a modern Fortran translation
of the adaptive rejection Metropolis algorithm in upstream `src/arms-R.c`. The
upstream source credits the original C ARMS code to Wally Gilks and the R port
to Giovanni Petris; those attributions are preserved here.

Shared numerical dependencies are referenced as sibling FPM path dependencies.
The `dlmMLE` mapping reuses the repository's top-level `optimx` translation. No
`optimx`, rfortran-core, rfortran-linalg, BLAS, LAPACK, ARPACK, or other
dependency source is copied into this package.
